## Context
Skills declare `model-level` and `effort` as launch intentions. With the LLM
choosing from the route grid (1064), these declarations go. Each PR edits the
tests it breaks, so CI stays green between waves.

## Scope
- Replace the declarations with a task description plus a pointer to the
  route skill in: `raid`, `healthcheck`, `molt`, `trace-doctor`, `hunt`,
  `release`, `biblio-saturation`, `critical-lit-review`, `external-peer-review`
  (and `external-peer-review/references/openrouter.md:34`).
- Fix `raid/SKILL.md:276-277` and `gaze/SKILL.md:678-679`, which describe the
  coder pin as `model-level: strong` (it is `model: strong`).
- Same PR: edit `tests/test_model_rightsizing.py:31-35` (fan-out bodies must
  declare `model-level`) and `tests/test_hunt_triage_prestep.py:106`.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] None of the listed skills mentions `model-level` or `effort:`
- [ ] The two tests are edited in this PR and pass
- [ ] `make skills-catalog` and `make check-skills-drift` pass
- [ ] `make check` passes
